# stdout:
Add addons to the profile's config and install them.

Each addon is a ref (github:owner/repo, wago:<id>) or its GitHub or
addons.wago.io link. Wago is read from its website, which needs no key, or
its official API with one: see knapsack sources set-api.
An addon already in config is left alone. Folders already in AddOns that
no addon owns are refused unless --force is given; folders another addon
owns are never replaced.

Usage:
  knapsack add <ref|url>... [flags]

Examples:
  knapsack add github:austinrr/baganator-mirror
  knapsack add https://github.com/austinrr/syndicator-mirror -p forever
  knapsack add https://addons.wago.io/addons/plater

Flags:
      --force            replace folders in AddOns that no addon owns
  -h, --help             help for add
  -p, --profile string   profile to act on (default $KNAPSACK_PROFILE, then the current profile)

Global Flags:
      --config string   use this config file instead of the default
  -v, --verbose         show progress and the underlying cause of errors
